('ic_active_listening_10', 'ic', 'Collaborative Communication', 'Active Listening', 'formal', 10, 'Tactical Empathy & W.A.I.T.', 'Study the ''W.A.I.T. (Why Am I Talking)'' framework and tactical empathy techniques for active listening.', 'During which recurring meeting are you most susceptible to speaking out of turn, and why?', 'Framework Study', 'Behavioral Model', 'Privately suggest two safe, constructive peers the employee could approach for the feedback exercise and encourage their participation.', 'What differences did you notice in group energy or engagement when you held back from speaking first?'),
('ic_transparent_sharing_70', 'ic', 'Collaborative Communication', 'Transparent Sharing', 'experiential', 70, 'Working Out Loud Weekly Sync', 'Start a ''working out loud'' habit by posting a brief, bulleted weekly update of your progress, blockers, and next steps in a public team channel.', 'What unanticipated help or resources did this visibility unlock?', 'Public Update', 'Async Channel', 'Be the first to comment on and celebrate the employee''s weekly public update to signal that this behavior is highly valued.', 'What feedback or unanticipated cross-functional assistance came in after sharing your working-out-loud update this week?'),
('ic_transparent_sharing_20', 'ic', 'Collaborative Communication', 'Transparent Sharing', 'social', 20, 'Cross-Functional Information Audit', 'Ask a cross-functional partner if there is a piece of data or context your team holds that would make their job easier if shared regularly.', 'Where were you making assumptions about what others already knew?', 'Stakeholder Inquiry', 'Cross-Team Alignment', 'Be the first to comment on and celebrate the employee''s weekly public update to signal that this behavior is highly valued.', 'What feedback or unanticipated cross-functional assistance came in after sharing your working-out-loud update this week?'),
('ic_transparent_sharing_10', 'ic', 'Collaborative Communication', 'Transparent Sharing', 'formal', 10, 'Radical Transparency Case Study', 'Read a case study on organizations that practice ''Radical Transparency'' and open-source internal communication.', 'What is the line between helpful transparency and over-communication in your current environment?', 'Case Study', 'Communication Strategy', 'Be the first to comment on and celebrate the employee''s weekly public update to signal that this behavior is highly valued.', 'What feedback or unanticipated cross-functional assistance came in after sharing your working-out-loud update this week?'),
